 "notes": {
  "height": "3 storeys, ~11.4 m (R7: pedestrian at the south mouth in 04 gives top ~11.4 m, storeys ~4.2/3.7/3.5).",
  "facades": "The road passage (OSM 44376249, in covered_streets) splits the building into a west and an east piece. South faces (04, 39): two round-arched windows in the top storey (one each side of the passage), one in the middle storey. Passage walls: the Sandrouni ceramics shop fronts (10, 43: dark teal steel-framed glazed doors, one round-arched and one segmental opening, oval bulkhead lamp) on the east wall at mid-length (wall side and position are unverified, R8); a wooden door and a small grilled window opposite. Nothing above the vault springing (hidden by the vault). North face of the west piece (05, 13, 21): plain, small windows.",
  "replaces": "OSM w1392907903 (removed in the profile, see its manual_buildings entry m_s01_armenian_2: same footprint with the south edge trimmed so the tunnel carve leaves no sliver across the mouth).",
  "keys": "facade keys are labels only (100+ = edge of the east piece); every facade carries its 'at' anchor, and the two passage-wall anchors sit 1.4 m inside their own piece so the walls (2.2 m apart) keep their own facade."
